 ### Fixed

+- `OrchestratorHooks.onError` now fires on every rejection inside a turn, not only when the thrown value satisfies `instanceof Error`. A non-`Error` rejection — a thrown string, a plain object, or `undefined` — is wrapped in an `Error` carrying a readable `message` and preserving the original thrown value on `error.cause`, while an existing `Error` instance still reaches `onError` unchanged and the caller still receives the original rejection untouched. **Migration note**: `onError` hooks that count failures or page on incidents will now observe non-`Error` rejections that were previously dropped silently; inspect `error.cause` if you need the raw non-`Error` value.
 - `onError` and `afterSession` hooks now fire when `beforeSession` throws, matching the guarantee the hook names imply. Previously, a throw from `beforeSession` escaped the `try`/`finally` block entirely, so neither hook ran. **Migration note**: if your `afterSession` hook assumed it would only be called after a full session turn, it will now also be called when `beforeSession` itself fails — the hook can inspect the session to detect this case (no entries beyond the initial user message will have been processed).

